# Design & Branding Manifesto

Before planning or changing any frontend code, visual design, styling, layout,
copy, component structure, or page-level information architecture, read:

- `docs/architecture/design-and-branding.md`

Treat that document as binding repository guidance. Non-negotiables:

- **Two registers.** Reflective content (journal, memories, identity, greeting)
  is editorial: serif `font-display`, generous spacing, soft radii. Operational
  content (tasks, timers, sessions, stats, settings) is instrument: mono
  `tabular-nums`, dense rows, hairline rules, restrained radii. Mixing registers
  across a screen is the brand; mixing them inside one component is a bug.
- **The AI gradient is rationed.** Use the shared `aiGradient` /
  `aiGradientLinear` tokens only, at the documented intensity tiers, with at most
  one full-bleed tier-1 surface visible at a time. Never re-author the gradient
  per surface.
- **Every AI surface** names its evidence, offers an action, allows manual
  override, and handles not-configured / signed-out / loading / stale /
  rate-limited / error states. The app must be fully usable with no API key.
- **Statistics require adjacent actions.** A metric with nothing to do about it
  gets cut, not decorated.
- **Palette tokens, never raw hexes.** The app ships System/Light/Dark only;
  every surface must work in light and dark. Named palettes were removed — do
  not bring them back.
- **No solid saturated brand-color content cards, no pastel placeholder blocks,
  no disconnected floating white lists.** Depth comes from tone and hairlines.
- **Frosted glass only** on floating/sticky chrome and AI surfaces; content cards
  stay opaque paper.
- **Mobile-first literally.** Unprefixed classes describe the phone; `lg:` adds a
  real two-column desktop shell with a wide primary column and a narrow context
  rail. Never the fixed 430px phone frame for new surfaces.
- **Journal and Memories are one record** distinguished by date precision
  (`exact` vs `approximate`), not two destinations.
- **Scope is decided in `docs/architecture/product-scope.md`.** Every kept
  feature (counters, never/avoid habits, check-only activities, streak flames,
  break days, memos, AI ordering with pins, start/stop time tracking, the
  sessions timeline, journal photos/places/opt-in daily clip, holiday and month
  banners, groups lifecycle, day navigation, en/pt, sync conflict review, backup,
  BYO-key AI) must be represented. Removed features (named palettes, quote
  footer, hearted-entry gradients, per-day pause, entry numbers, hidden group
  activities, timed⇄untimed conversion, guest mode, task-order screen, 7-day
  edit lock, configurable day-reset hour — days end at midnight) must not be
  designed for. Changing either list requires updating
  `product-scope.md` first.
- **Copy in both `en` and `pt`**, through i18n. Hardcoded English is a defect.
- **Keyboard equivalent for every pointer interaction**; labels on icon-only
  controls.

Any intentional departure must update
`docs/architecture/design-and-branding.md` first and explain the changed product
tradeoff before implementation.
